.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/mz Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "MZ - Modernize node\&.js"
.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP [][license-url] \fR\fP

.PP
Modernize node\&.js to current ECMAScript specifications! node\&.js will not update their API to ES6+ \fRfor a while\fP\&. This library is a wrapper for various aspects of node\&.js' API\&.
.SH "Installation and Usage"
.PP
Set \fRmz\fP as a dependency and install it\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm i mz
.fi
.PP

.PP
Then prefix the relevant \fRrequire()\fPs with \fRmz/\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
var fs = require('mz/fs')

fs\&.exists(__filename)\&.then(function (exists) {
  if (exists) // do something
})
.fi
.PP

.PP
With ES2017, this will allow you to use async functions cleanly with node's core API:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const fs = require('mz/fs')


async function doSomething () {
  if (await fs\&.exists(__filename)) // do something
}
.fi
.PP
.SH "Promisification"
.PP
Many node methods are converted into promises\&. Any properties that are deprecated or aren't asynchronous will simply be proxied\&. The modules wrapped are:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRchild_process\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRcrypto\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdns\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRfs\fP (uses \fRgraceful-fs\fP if available)
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRreadline\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRzlib\fP
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
var exec = require('mz/child_process')\&.exec

exec('node \-\-version')\&.then(function (stdout) {
  console\&.log(stdout)
})
.fi
.PP
.SH "Promise Engine"
.PP
\fRmz\fP uses \fR\fRany-promise\fP\fP\&.
.SH "FAQ"
.PP
.SS "Can I use this in production?"
Yes, Node 4\&.x ships with stable promises support\&. For older engines, you should probably install your own promise implementation and register it with \fRrequire('any-promise/register')('bluebird')\fP\&.
.SS "Will this make my app faster?"
Nope, probably slower actually\&.
.SS "Can I add more features?"
Sure\&. Open an issue\&.

.PP
Currently, the plans are to eventually support:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
New APIs in node\&.js that are not available in older versions of node
.IP "\(bu" 2
ECMAScript7 Streams 
.PP

